# .gitignore — MowCodeGamingBoteY
#
# Grouped with reasons, per STANDARDS_OTE_WAY_OF_WORKING.md §2: this file doubles
# as documentation of WHY something is out of the repo.
#
# It exists BEFORE the first `npm install` on purpose. That ordering is a rule
# because the opposite already cost real time elsewhere.

# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Never tracked. Once, 140 dependency files were committed under a test folder,
# and because a `file:` dependency is an npm SYMLINK, one landed as an embedded
# git repository — which a clone silently cannot fetch.
node_modules/

# ── Lockfiles ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each project regenerates its own via `npm install`.
package-lock.json
**/package-lock.json

# ── Secrets / local config ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Discord bot token and the database password live in config.json.
# config.example.json is the TRACKED, documented shape with empty secrets.
# No .env in this project — JSON config is the convention (§3).
# The legacy Python bot hardcoded a live bot token in source
# (Gaming Bot/CsGamingBot.py:41). This line is what makes that impossible here.
config.json
configs/

# ── Logs ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Run-scoped log files — the descendant of the legacy debug_msg/YYYYMMDD.txt
# folder. They contain Discord user ids, message content and query text.
logs/
*.log

# ── Editor / OS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .history/ is exactly what put 13,652 copies of a live token into the legacy
# tree. Deleting the live file does not remove those.
.history/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
